    "loc": {
      "type": "bella-location",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Virtual staging & 3D rendering · Florida",
        "heading": "Virtual Staging for Home Builders: Florida New Construction & Listings",
        "lede": "Virtual staging is a digital marketing technique for real estate: a designer adds furniture and décor to photos of empty or cleared rooms so potential buyers can visualize the space, with no furniture delivered to the property. Bella's designers stage Florida new construction, spec homes and model homes for home builders and developers — and listings for agents — in 24 to 48 hours, from {price:virtual-staging} a photo, and render homes that aren't built yet from your plans.",
        "cta_label": "Stage my listing — from {price:virtual-staging}",
        "cta_link": "/products/virtual-staging",
        "alt_label": "3D renderings for builders",
        "alt_link": "/products/3d-rendering-service-for-architectural-visualization",
        "city": "Florida",
        "market_heading": "Why virtual staging works for Florida home builders",
        "market_text": "<p>Florida builders sell to buyers who often aren't here yet: northern relocations, retirees and second-home buyers shortlist new construction from photos, and a vacant spec home with white tile floors doesn't sell a Florida lifestyle to someone scrolling from another state. Virtual staging furnishes those listing photos so buyers can see scale, flow and how each room lives — the first impression that decides whether they book a visit.</p><p>It also removes the logistics that slow a builder down. There is no furniture to move into an active construction site, no rental contract per home and no crew to schedule across a community, so spec homes and quick move-ins get online faster. Designers can show the same floor plan in more than one style, keep one consistent look across every listing in a community, and match the design to each region's buyers — coastal on the Gulf Coast, contemporary in Miami, transitional in family communities around Orlando and Jacksonville.</p><p>Before a home is built, there is nothing to photograph. Bella's <a href=\"/products/3d-rendering-service-for-architectural-visualization\">3D rendering service</a> turns your plans into photorealistic exteriors and interiors from {price:3d-rendering} an image, so you can pre-sell from plans, fill the sales center and launch community pages before construction is complete. Our <a href=\"/pages/home-builder-marketing\">home builder marketing guide</a> covers the full pre-sale playbook.</p><p>Agents use the same service on resale listings. 97% of buyers use the internet in their home search (NAR), and in NAR's 2025 Profile of Home Staging, 83% of buyers' agents said staging made it easier for a buyer to visualize the property as a future home — which is why virtual staging works so well in a state with so many vacant, seasonal, investment and second-home properties.</p>",
        "local_heading": "Florida builder staging: Tampa, Orlando, Miami and Jacksonville",
        "local_text": "<p><strong>Virtual staging Tampa Bay.</strong> Spec homes and new communities from Tampa and St. Petersburg to Sarasota get airy transitional and coastal staging, with files sized for Stellar MLS. Agents listing resale homes can also see our <a href=\"/pages/virtual-staging-in-tampa\">virtual staging in Tampa</a> page.</p><p><strong>Orlando.</strong> Family-sized floor plans in new communities are staged to show how bonus rooms, lofts and lanais are used — the rooms buyers can't picture empty.</p><p><strong>Virtual staging Miami &amp; South Florida.</strong> Condo and townhome developments from Miami to Fort Lauderdale and Palm Beach get a clean contemporary look, with files ready for the Miami REALTORS® MLS. It's a lower-cost alternative to physical home staging: Miami developers can stage every vacant unit in the photos, or render the ones still under construction.</p><p><strong>Jacksonville.</strong> New construction across Northeast Florida is staged warm and transitional, with volume pricing for builders listing a community at once — 5% off at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+.</p><p>Outdoor space gets staged as living space rather than as an afterthought — lanais, pool decks and screened porches are where Florida listings win the scroll. Our design team works online, so there's no site visit or delivery to schedule anywhere in the state.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Where we work most",
        "hoods": "Tampa, St. Petersburg, Sarasota, Orlando, Miami, Fort Lauderdale, Palm Beach, Naples, Jacksonville",
        "cred_text": "From {price:virtual-staging} a photo · 3D renders from {price:3d-rendering} · 24–48 hour staging · Real designers, never AI"
      }
    },
